From b87ae6e6019370a6b70a47186b3403c52e93e96e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 14:35:11 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] drm: bridge: cadence: add HDMI audio support to
 MHDP8501

The MHDP8501 firmware carries audio in the HDMI stream, but the driver
posted as v20 has no way to feed it: the audio code was dropped between
v1 and v2 of the series and the promised follow-up never arrived. The
leftover "select DRM_CDNS_AUDIO" in Kconfig refers to a symbol that no
longer exists anywhere in the tree.

Wire the audio path up through the DRM bridge HDMI audio infrastructure
rather than registering an hdmi-codec platform device by hand, so the
core owns the codec device, the ELD and the audio infoframe. The sample
source, smpl2pckt and FIFO programming is taken from the v1 driver,
which in turn came from the Rockchip cdn-dp driver for the same IP.

Only I2S playback is wired up. The internal S/PDIF path needs the SPDIF
clock and reset that the i.MX8MQ binding does not describe, and DP audio
needs its own bridge op, so both are left out.

The audio infoframe takes packet memory entry 3; entries 0 to 2 are
already spoken for by AVI, SPD and vendor.
